[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2472894192","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99162#issuecomment-2472894192","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99162","id":2472894192,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TZV7w","user":{"login":"justofisker","id":37525404,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NTI1NDA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37525404?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justofisker","html_url":"https://github.com/justofisker","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justofisker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justofisker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justofisker/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justofisker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justofisker/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justofisker/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justofisker/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justofisker/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justofisker/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-13T09:00:52Z","updated_at":"2024-11-13T09:00:52Z","body":"Bisected to 08947d366fba19fe28733538eec0dafe11304032","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2472894192/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2472903874","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99162#issuecomment-2472903874","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99162","id":2472903874,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TZYTC","user":{"login":"justofisker","id":37525404,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NTI1NDA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37525404?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justofisker","html_url":"https://github.com/justofisker","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justofisker/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justofisker/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justofisker/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justofisker/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justofisker/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justofisker/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justofisker/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justofisker/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justofisker/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-13T09:05:04Z","updated_at":"2024-11-13T09:05:04Z","body":"Also made a non-mono [mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/17729527/mrp.zip)\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2472903874/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2473474554","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99162#issuecomment-2473474554","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99162","id":2473474554,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Tbjn6","user":{"login":"RandomShaper","id":11797174,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk3MTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11797174?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper","html_url":"https://github.com/RandomShaper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-13T12:28:41Z","updated_at":"2024-11-13T12:28:41Z","body":"In 4,4, a thread-safe `RID_Owner`s has a limit on the amount of `RID`s it can hold, not changeable at runtime. The constructor has a parameter for that, that defaults to `262144`.\r\n\r\nThat's exactly the case of the `RenderingSceneCull::instance_owner`, the one relevant to the MRP. The MRP tries to create 1.2 M instances, which is above the limit. If the MRP tried to create `262144` or less instances, the project would run fine.\r\n\r\nIf a real-world project really needs to instantiate that many objects, we could add a project setting. It this is a purely theoretical test, I'd just close this as a no-issue.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2473474554/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2474398284","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99162#issuecomment-2474398284","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99162","id":2474398284,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TfFJM","user":{"login":"MilesRomanum","id":19277050,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjc3MDUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19277050?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum","html_url":"https://github.com/MilesRomanum","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-13T18:19:22Z","updated_at":"2024-11-13T18:19:22Z","body":"That makes sense. How can I set it as a project setting? I do need it to animate around 30k humanoids with 30 joints and composite models {for clothes on top of the base model)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2474398284/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2474405816","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99162#issuecomment-2474405816","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99162","id":2474405816,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TfG-4","user":{"login":"MilesRomanum","id":19277050,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjc3MDUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19277050?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum","html_url":"https://github.com/MilesRomanum","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-13T18:23:25Z","updated_at":"2024-11-13T18:23:25Z","body":"Fwiw, I think the default limit of 256k is definitely on the low side for a pc game. Even with my project that instanciate the visualinstance with a mid poly model 30k times, the memory usage only got to 6gig which is well within spec for a typical pc game.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2474405816/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2474598453","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99162#issuecomment-2474598453","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99162","id":2474598453,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Tf2A1","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-13T19:44:20Z","updated_at":"2024-11-13T19:44:20Z","body":"@MilesRomanum A typical object count budget for AAA games is in the low tens of thousands. When you start needing more than that you should be exploring ways of batching together work. For example, using MultiMeshInstance or particles to control thousands of instances at once. \r\n\r\nAlso consider using multiple mesh surfaces instead of multiple instances for composite models. By using individual instances for each item you will be guaranteeing performance issues","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2474598453/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2474703505","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99162#issuecomment-2474703505","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99162","id":2474703505,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TgPqR","user":{"login":"MilesRomanum","id":19277050,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjc3MDUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19277050?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum","html_url":"https://github.com/MilesRomanum","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-13T20:18:45Z","updated_at":"2024-11-13T20:18:45Z","body":"I can probably use multi-mesh surface for composite models. \r\nBut regarding object count budget, my game resolves around modelling armies of npc with animations. \r\ninstancing limbs of npc has been how i make it run with a good framerate, and with some lod and animation sampling techniques it actually works really well with rendering server.\r\nThis vid below is an example of the game in motion. There is a lot more off screen of course, but fwiw, it's running at 170fps so Godot can clearly handle it.\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e877d950-6ca8-405e-8512-cfc3bf095e29\r\n![s](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8c7350d8-d4fe-43cb-b63c-907a6dd4354f)\r\n\r\nI want to be able to allow artists to create their animations into gltf formats, which I think would be difficult with the multimeshinstance or particles\r\n\r\nI saw the commit that changed it and I understand why it is in place. Would there be a way to make the rid_owner max configurable? I suppose worst case would be me learning to compile just changing that constant, but would appreciate it if it can be configured because I think there might be other devs who also appreciate it.\r\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2474703505/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2475022264","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99162#issuecomment-2475022264","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99162","id":2475022264,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Thde4","user":{"login":"MilesRomanum","id":19277050,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjc3MDUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19277050?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum","html_url":"https://github.com/MilesRomanum","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-13T23:20:14Z","updated_at":"2024-11-13T23:20:14Z","body":"I also dont mind using the not thread safe version of rendering server if that's available. I already do a long of batching and sycnrhonization in my own code to make sure renderingserver only get called on a single thread. Is there a flag to make renderingserver not thread safe? thanks","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2475022264/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2475880426","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99162#issuecomment-2475880426","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99162","id":2475880426,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Tku_q","user":{"login":"RandomShaper","id":11797174,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk3MTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11797174?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper","html_url":"https://github.com/RandomShaper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-14T09:49:40Z","updated_at":"2024-11-14T09:49:40Z","body":"The unsafe thread model for rendering was never a thing in Godot 4. In fact, I've made a PR that makes that explicit: #98383.\r\n\r\nThat said, it would be technically possible to bring it back. However, that would add some extra burden. For instance, already very complex areas of the engine, such as the `ResourceLoader`, would require extra logic . My point, ultimately, is that we won't likely want to support something like that unless it's deemed worth it.\r\n\r\n(For the records, there's an alternative implementation path that may make things a little easier, if still complex. I'm leaving it here for the records. It would be optimizing the engine for threadless builds in a way that it assumes everything happens on the same thread. That way, everything would be \"unsafe\" by default and it'd only be a matter of still allowing such kind of build to spawn threads. Again, the risk-benefit statement stands.)","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2475880426/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2476302131","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99162#issuecomment-2476302131","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99162","id":2476302131,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TmV8z","user":{"login":"MilesRomanum","id":19277050,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjc3MDUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19277050?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum","html_url":"https://github.com/MilesRomanum","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MilesRomanum/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-14T13:01:51Z","updated_at":"2024-11-14T13:01:51Z","body":"Thats fair. If it is possible (and not require additional long term support), Im just interested in the simplest way for an end user like me to be able to allocate a bit more than the initial default. \r\n\r\nThe approach may be unorthodox, but it has allowed me to have really good performance doing things this way, leveraging multitheading and caching for skeletal animations. If there is a simple and cheap way for this to be supported, I would be immensely grateful ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2476302131/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2476393087","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99162#issuecomment-2476393087","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99162","id":2476393087,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TmsJ_","user":{"login":"RandomShaper","id":11797174,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk3MTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11797174?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper","html_url":"https://github.com/RandomShaper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/orgs","repos_u