1Z","updated_at":"2024-11-14T23:30:31Z","body":"I would love to give making this change a shot. I want to get into developing for the engine and this seems like a simple enough PR to work on!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2477618943/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2712196490","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99162#issuecomment-2712196490","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99162","id":2712196490,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hqNWK","user":{"login":"bikemurt","id":23486102,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzNDg2MTAy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23486102?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt","html_url":"https://github.com/bikemurt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikemurt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-11T01:08:43Z","updated_at":"2025-03-11T04:01:44Z","body":"Just chiming in here that this issue immediately affects my project when migrating to 4.4. In my case I am making heavy use of batching already with multimeshes, it's just that I pre-allocate all possible rendering instances for higher levels of LOD which get swapped in (this hasn't costed too much in memory, I'm still well under a couple of gigs).\n\nIn my case should I wait for this project setting to get exposed? Or do I bite the bullet and re-architect to try and manage rendering server instances better?\n\nEdit: unfortunately after profiling, I'm seeing my draw calls 4x after migrating to 4.4. I took a lot of time and effort to optimize under 4.3, so I may have to open another issue. I'll wait to see if anyone else (who made extensive use of the rendering server) has similar problems. It may be just an implementation thing on my part.\n\nEdit2: Found my rendering bug. Issue posted here https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103954","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2712196490/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]